---
/*
 * Closing CTA. Copy verbatim from docs/shep-design/README.md,
 * "Screens > 1. Landing page > CTA footer", except "1030 tests" -> "Over a
 * thousand tests": that literal count already drifted once (README.md's
 * own copy made this exact fix — "Tested by trying to break it. Over a
 * thousand tests..." — so this page follows the source-of-truth voice
 * instead of reintroducing a number that decays every phase).
 *
 * The old ink footer bar (license line + a Docs link) and the decorative
 * bobbing flock row are gone: the license lives with the docs, the nav
 * already links Docs, and the living pasture behind this section carries
 * far more sheep than a static row ever did. The page now ends on the
 * scene itself.
 */
---

<section class="cta">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="board">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="copy">
          <h2>Build it and tell me<br />what breaks.</h2>
          <p>
            Rust 1.88 or newer, edition 2024. Over a thousand tests, and every
            task ends with a mutation pass: break a line on purpose, confirm a
            test goes red, put it back.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="buttons">
          <a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep" class="btn butter press" style="--shadow-offset:6px; --shadow-color:var(--ink); --press-offset:3px;">
            Clone the repo
          </a>
          <a href="/docs" class="btn cream press" style="--shadow-offset:6px; --shadow-color:var(--ink); --press-offset:3px;">
            Read the docs
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cta {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 7;
    /* Rides the sky stage (see Lexicon.astro); the closing board below is
       what keeps the copy readable over the scenery. clip, not hidden, as
       everywhere inside the stage. */
    padding: 70px 0 110px;
    overflow-x: clip;
  }

  .inner {
    max-width: 1240px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 28px;
  }

  /* Same whitewashed-plank language as the feature cards (the recipe note
     lives in SignpostCard.astro): ink copy was unreadable straight over
     the hills and the walking flock. 48px period, two 24px body lines. */
  .board {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border: 4px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 26px;
    box-shadow: 9px 9px 0 var(--shadow);
    padding: 44px 46px;
    background-image:
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        rgba(23, 37, 28, 0) 0 45px,
        rgba(23, 37, 28, 0.12) 45px 48px
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12) 0 4px,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 8px 48px
      );
    background-position-y: 10px;
  }

  .board::before,
  .board::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 15px;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .board::before {
    left: 15px;
  }

  .board::after {
    right: 15px;
  }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: 36px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: "Bricolage Grotesque", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.6vw, 60px);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .copy p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .buttons {
    display: grid;
    gap: 13px;
  }

  .btn {
    font-family: "Bricolage Grotesque", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 17px;
    border: 4px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 17px 30px;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-align: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .btn.butter {
    background: var(--butter);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .btn.cream {
    background: var(--fleece);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* Responsive first pass (docs/shep-design/README.md, "Responsive"):
     single-column stack below ~640px instead of squeezing the button
     column into whatever space is left beside the heading. */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .buttons {
      justify-items: stretch;
    }

    .board {
      padding: 32px 26px;
    }
  }
</style>
